From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] renderer text engine: keep fill ops in text color

In TTF_DrawRendererText(), underline/strikethrough draw operations can be
batched as fill sequences (texture == NULL, image_type invalid). The current
color branch treats all non-alpha sequences as color glyph images and forces
RGB to white, so decoration lines render white for non-white text.

Use text color for fill sequences, while preserving the existing behavior for
color glyph textures.

diff --git a/src/SDL_renderer_textengine.c b/src/SDL_renderer_textengine.c
--- a/src/SDL_renderer_textengine.c
+++ b/src/SDL_renderer_textengine.c
@@
         SDL_FColor color;
-        if (sequence->image_type == TTF_IMAGE_ALPHA) {
+        if (sequence->image_type == TTF_IMAGE_ALPHA || sequence->texture == NULL) {
             SDL_copyp(&color, &text->internal->color);
         } else {
             // Don't alter the color data in the image
             color.r = 1.0f;
             color.g = 1.0f;
